0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 58.0 691.0 Tm (* "What barriers make it hard to accept a shelter offer or hold a job?") Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 58.0 672.6 Tm (* "What might we be overlooking because we only see one part of the problem?") Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 48.0 654.2 Tm (Useful conversation agreements) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 58.0 640.8 Tm (* Speak about people as individuals. No name-calling, jokes at someone's expense, or sweeping labels.) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 58.0 622.4 Tm (* Use "I" statements and questions. Distinguish what you saw from what you inferred.) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 58.0 604.0 Tm (* Safety, housing, treatment, neighborhood conditions, costs, and dignity may all matter; participants) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 48.0 590.6 Tm (may disagree on the solutions.) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 58.0 572.2 Tm (* Nobody is required to debate their own lived experience.) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 48.0 553.8 Tm (If a discussion gets heated: "We might disagree about the solution. What outcome are we both hoping) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 48.0 540.4 Tm (for ... and what could help us tell whether it's working?") Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 48.0 522.0 Tm (Grounding in the Invisible People toolkit) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 48.0 508.6 Tm (The 2025 messaging toolkit explains that people may respond to the same housing solution for different reasons,) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 48.0 495.2 Tm (including community wellbeing, safety, and responsible use of resources. This guide adapts that insight for listening) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 48.0 481.8 Tm (and education ... not for teaching demographic stereotypes or running a persuasion workshop.) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 48.0 463.4 Tm (CHICO CAMPOUT FOR COMPASSION 2026 NOVEMBER 14 * HOST PACKET) Tj ET
0.80 0.90 0.91 RG .6 w 48 433.0 m 564 433.0 l S
0 0.16 0.29 rg BT /F2 11.60 Tf 1 0 0 1 48.0 428.0 Tm (08 * DIRECT SUPPORT) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 48.0 403.8 Tm (Optional basic-needs drive ... no central) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 48.0 390.4 Tm (fund) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 48.0 377.0 Tm (The awareness program itself does not collect money or administer a shared fund. Participation is free,) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 48.0 363.6 Tm (and giving is entirely optional.) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 48.0 345.2 Tm (Simple direct-donation model) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 58.0 331.8 Tm (* Each host asks one existing Chico-area service organization what supplies are useful right now.) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 58.0 313.4 Tm (* The receiving organization approves a short list and a delivery location/time.) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 58.0 295.0 Tm (* Participants bring only approved items; sort safely and respectfully.) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 58.0 276.6 Tm (* The host delivers items directly to that organization and confirms receipt.) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 58.0 258.2 Tm (* Those who want to donate money do so directly to the nonprofit, not to Campout for Compassion.) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 48.0 239.8 Tm (Possible items ... only if requested) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 48.0 226.4 Tm (New socks, basic hygiene items, unopened shelf-stable food, seasonal clothing, menstrual supplies, or) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 48.0 213.0 Tm (other items named by the partner. Do not assume that every program wants the same supplies or) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 48.0 199.6 Tm (accepts used items.) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 48.0 181.2 Tm (Good partners to approach) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 48.0 167.8 Tm (Local shelters, outreach teams, housing organizations, youth service providers, food pantries, and other) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 48.0 154.4 Tm (existing programs. Contact them before putting their name or logo on materials.) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 48.0 136.0 Tm (Keep the emphasis right: A bag of supplies may be helpful, but it is not a replacement for stable housing.) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 48.0 122.6 Tm (This event is about understanding homelessness and valuing our neighbors.) Tj ET
0.17 0.25 0.30 rg BT /F1 9.35 Tf 1 0 0 1 48.0 104.2 Tm (CHICO CAMPOUT FOR COMPASSION 2026 NOVEMBER 14 * HOST PACKET) Tj ET
